# Build patterns (always on)

**Golden sentence:** New behavior is a **pure** transform + a **registry** row (when N ≥ 2 kinds) + an **orchestrator** with injected `deps`, called by thin UI / HTTP / MCP / CLI adapters. Never `if (projectId === …)` / `if (provider === …)` / `if (harness === …)` business logic in hosts, and never a UI-only verb an agent can't reach.

Pairs with `architecture/harness-shell-fidelity.mdc` (peers own loops; Studio is the shell) and `architecture/code-structure.mdc` (when to split the result).

## Layers — who owns what

| Layer | Owns | Never |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `*-pure.ts` / `*-logic.ts` | Transforms, validation, projections, ranking | `fetch`, `fs`, `document`, env reads |
| `*-registry-pure.ts` | Id → implementation / policy row | Business I/O; host-only switches |
| `*-orchestrator.ts` | Sequence pure + registry + injected deps | Business rules inline; hard-coded I/O |
| `*-connector.ts` / `*-mount.ts` / handlers / MCP / CLI | Wire orchestrator to HTTP/DOM/XState/MCP/CLI | Duplicate logic from pure / orchestrator |

```typescript
// ✅ orchestrator — deps injected, pure core testable
export async function loadProjectFilesOrchestrator(
  deps: { listFiles: typeof listProjectFiles },
  input: { root: string; subPath: string },
) {
  return deps.listFiles(input.root, input.subPath);
}

// ✅ test — text/oracle, no server
const files = await loadProjectFilesOrchestrator(
  { listFiles: async () => [{ name: "a.mdx", path: "content/a.mdx", type: "file" }] },
  { root: "/tmp", subPath: "content" },
);
```

## Registries (when N ≥ 2 kinds)

```typescript
// ✅ registry lookup — add a row, not a host branch
export const MEMORY_IMPORT_PROJECTORS = { hermes: {…}, letta: {…} } as const;
export function getMemoryImportProjector(id: string) { … }

// ❌ one-off in handler
if (provider === "hermes") { … } else if (provider === "letta") { … }
```

Same pattern: harness vision modes, tool catalogs, canvas window kinds, providers.

## Pure branching — `switch` over `if` chains

In `*-pure.ts` / `*-logic.ts`, branch on a **discriminant** (kind, status, phase, mode, enum, union tag, finite string id) with **`switch`** — never `if` / `else if` chains on that value.

| Use | Form |
| --- | --- |
| Discriminant / finite tag | `switch (kind) { case …: … default: … }` |
| Exhaustive TS union | `default: { const _x: never = kind; return _x }` |
| Early guard / predicate | `if (!x) return …` / `if (a && b)` — **OK** (not a discriminant chain) |
| N ≥ 2 kinds → behavior map | Prefer **registry** (`*-registry-pure`) over a long `switch` body |

```typescript
// ✅ discriminant → switch
switch (phase) {
  case "unbound":
  case "loading":
    return "pending";
  case "ready":
    return empty ? "empty" : "log";
  case "error":
    return "error";
  default: {
    const _exhaustive: never = phase;
    return _exhaustive;
  }
}

// ❌ same discriminant as if/else if
if (phase === "unbound" || phase === "loading") return "pending";
else if (phase === "ready") return empty ? "empty" : "log";
else if (phase === "error") return "error";

// ✅ guard stays if
if (!input) return null;
if (typeof raw !== "string") return "system";
```

**Scope:** new pure code + any pure file you touch — convert discriminant chains to `switch` in the same PR. Do not leave `else if (kind === …)` in pure modules you edit.

## No one-offs

**Golden sentence:** New behavior is a **registry row** or **config map** + **pure** transform + **orchestrator** (deps) + thin adapter.

| Smell | Fail if | Do instead |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **Project-id branch** | `if (projectId === 'demo-blog')` in engine/shell | `project.json` maps / kind registries |
| **Provider / peer branch in host** | `if (provider === 'hermes')` in HTTP/MCP/CLI | `*-registry-pure` projector map + lookup |
| **Logic in the adapter** | Retrieve / forge / import rules inside `handlers/*` or `mcp-orchestrator` cases | `*-orchestrator.ts` with injected `deps`; adapter only parses I/O |

**UI ↔ CLI ↔ MCP parity:** same orchestrator. Third copy of a rule = extract.

### Config / map SoT (projects)

| Need | Source of truth |
| --- | --- |
| Nav sections + Live URL map | `project.json` → `nav` + `route` |
| Hosting preview origin | `project.json` → `hosting.prod_url` |
| Behavior from inputs | `@glassbox-studio/studio-core` pure + registries |

## DRY & extensibility (other operators)

**Golden sentences:**

1. **DRY** — one source of truth per concern; UI and CLI call the same API / pure path.
2. **Abstract for the next user** — defaults are opinionated; behavior is swappable via config, registry, layout, or plugin — not a hard-coded single-operator tree.
3. **Changeable up and down the stack** — tokens → chrome layout → panels → harness → headless API; each layer has a declared seam.

| Do | Don't |
| --- | --- |
| Shared pure + API; thin UI/CLI adapters | Copy business rules into `app.tsx` **and** a CLI script |
| Declarative maps (`project.json`, left-rail layout, plugin contrib) | Paste the same branch in three hosts |
| Extract when a second caller appears | "Just one more" duplicate "for speed" |

Assume someone else will reorder the left rail, add non-demo projects, or run headless. Declare the seam at **each** layer you touch (tokens, chrome layout, project config, API/CLI, harness/tools). If the answer is "only by editing our private fork," stop and add a seam. Detail: `docs/architecture/studio-plugins.md`.

## UI ↔ MCP ↔ CLI parity (ship bar)

**Golden sentence:** If a human can do it in Studio UI, an agent can do it via **MCP catalog** (and therefore CLI + Voice). No UI-only product verbs.

Audience: **Studio Host / chrome / DeskPane apps** (`apps/studio`, `packages/studio/*`, Voice). Ideal-stack Live pages follow HTTP/loaders — not this catalog.

ADR: [0012](../../docs/adr/0012-section-provider-tools.md). Gate: `app-tools-face-pure.ts`.

```
UI click  →  same orchestrator  →  MCP tool id  →  CLI `studio mcp <id>`  →  Voice/Chat job
```

| Face | Required | Fail if |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **Panel** | DeskPane / settings / chrome | Feature only in a Handle with no Host path |
| **HTTP** | Handler on the orchestrator | UI `fetch` that MCP cannot call |
| **MCP** | Row in `tool-catalog-pure.ts` | Open-only (`studio.nav`) for a new app's **job** |
| **CLI** | `studio mcp <action>` (named subcommand optional) | UI-only side door |
| **Voice / Chat** | Dispatch that catalog id | Voice-only tool that UI/MCP lack |

`studio.nav` opens/focuses windows — it does **not** replace domain verbs (`messages.send`, `notes.write`, `calendar.create`, …). Named CLI is optional (`studio chat`, `studio sheets`); `studio mcp` is enough to ship.

**Allowed non-catalog** (agents use files / `shell.run` / `studio.nav` / `studio.home.patch` instead): CodeMirror caret / xterm keystrokes, DeskPane drag-resize by pixels, true DOM scratch (focus ring, timer ids).

## Agent checklist (every AI / domain / UI edit)

- [ ] New behavior has a pure function (or extends one) before glue code
- [ ] Multiple kinds/providers → **registry** row, not host `if`
- [ ] Pure discriminant branches use **`switch`**; guards stay `if`
- [ ] Orchestrator accepts `deps` / `options` — not hard-coded imports of I/O
- [ ] HTTP, MCP, and CLI (when product-facing) call the **same** orchestrator
- [ ] New mutating / multi-step path → `*-orchestrator.ts` with `deps`
- [ ] Vitest (or terminal oracle) covers pure + orchestrator (+ registry lookup) paths
- [ ] No `if (projectId|provider|harnessId === '…')` for **behavior** in hosts
- [ ] Catalog id in `tool-catalog-pure.ts` (+ schema) for every new UI verb
- [ ] Canvas window → `APP_TOOLS_FACE` prefixes (no new `open-only` debt)
- [ ] Gate green: `vitest run app-tools-face-pure`

